---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE_URL } from "../consts";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms and conditions governing your use of Power BI Tutorials."
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <div class="content-width">
      <span class="page-eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: July 19, 2026</p>

      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of
        {SITE_URL} (the "Site"). By accessing the Site, you agree to be
        bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Use of the Site</h2>
      <p>
        Power BI Tutorials provides tutorials and educational content about Power BI,
        DAX, and Power Query. You may use the Site for personal, non-commercial
        educational purposes. You agree not to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the Site in any way that violates applicable laws or regulations</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of the Site</li>
        <li>Interfere with the proper functioning of the Site, including advertising systems</li>
        <li>Scrape, copy, or republish substantial portions of content without permission</li>
        <li>Use automated systems (bots, crawlers) to access the Site in a way that sends more requests than a human reasonably could</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Site's content — including articles, code samples, diagrams, and
        design — is owned by Power BI Tutorials and protected by copyright and other
        intellectual property laws. You may:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>View and read content for personal learning</li>
        <li>Share links to individual pages</li>
        <li>Quote brief excerpts with attribution and a link back to the source</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You may not reproduce, republish, or distribute full articles without
        prior written permission. DAX code samples provided in tutorials are
        released under the MIT license and may be used freely in your own
        projects.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Educational content disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        All tutorials and content on the Site are provided for educational
        purposes only. While we strive for accuracy, Power BI and DAX are
        complex tools that change frequently. You are responsible for
        validating any formula, pattern, or technique against your own data
        before relying on it in production environments.
      </p>

      <h2>4. No professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on the Site constitutes professional, financial, or technical
        consulting advice. We are not liable for any losses or damages
        arising from the application of techniques described in our content.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Advertising and affiliate disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        The Site is supported by advertising (Google AdSense) and may include
        affiliate links. Advertising and affiliate relationships do not
        influence editorial content or product comparisons. Where a link is
        affiliate, we disclose it. We only recommend tools and services we
        have genuinely evaluated.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-party links and services</h2>
      <p>
        The Site contains links to third-party websites and references
        third-party products (e.g., Microsoft Power BI). We are not
        responsible for the content, policies, or practices of third parties.
        Your use of third-party services is subject to their respective terms.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Power BI Tutorials and its authors
        shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
        consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of data, arising
        from your use of the Site, including but not limited to damages
        resulting from following any tutorial, formula, or recommendation.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold Power BI Tutorials harmless from any claims,
        damages, or expenses arising from your misuse of the Site or
        violation of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to the Site and Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may modify or discontinue any part of the Site at any time. We
        may revise these Terms by posting an updated version on this page.
        Continued use of the Site after changes constitutes acceptance of
        the revised Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by applicable laws without regard to
        conflict-of-law principles. Any disputes will be resolved in the
        competent courts of the applicable jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> or
        email <a href="mailto:legal@powerbitutorials.com">legal@powerbitutorials.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page { padding: 56px 0 80px; }
  .page-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--c-accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .legal-page h1 { font-size: 2.2rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .updated { color: var(--c-text-dim); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .legal-page h2 { margin-top: 2.2em; font-size: 1.3rem; }
  .legal-page p { font-size: 0.95rem; }
</style>
